# The Harbor rules

- Read `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` before editing.
- Treat Harbor as an original design. NetFin is a distribution reference only;
  do not copy its code, assets, wording, fonts, or visual identity.
- Develop modular CSS under `src/css/`, then run `npm run build:css`.
- Never hand-edit root `theme.css`. It is the complete generated stylesheet that
  Jellyfin imports through jsDelivr.
- The final stable URL is
  `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/NerdyPorcupine-Squared/the-harbor@main/theme.css`.
  Use an immutable commit SHA instead of `main` for release-candidate testing.
- Keep Core CSS-only. Put future JavaScript in a separate optional JS Injector
  package; never make Core depend on JavaScript or Media Bar Enhanced.
- Keep the home page trailer-led when Media Bar exists and naturally compact
  when it does not.
- Preserve Jellyfin behavior and semantics. Never change playback state,
  network requests, result order, lazy loading, or essential-control behavior.
- Use parchment-dominant browsing surfaces with restrained cartography; keep
  header and drawer navigation structurally dark, preserve full-color artwork,
  keep cinematic media regions dark, and keep the player dark and unobstructed.
- Use test-driven development. Observe a meaningful RED failure before feature
  implementation, then run focused tests, `npm run verify:core`, and affected
  Playwright specs.
- Do not weaken tests, hide controls, or suppress overflow to manufacture a
  pass. Fix the underlying UI.
- Maintain keyboard focus, 40x40 mobile hit targets, 200% zoom, reduced motion,
  forced colors, and coarse-pointer support.
- Use sanitized fixtures with invented nautical labels and generated art only.
- Never commit personal information, real server data, private media, secrets,
  machine paths, screenshots, logs, `docs/superpowers/**`, or `.superpowers/**`
  to a public candidate.
- Do not tag `v1.0.0` or state that Harbor is real-server validated until the
  owner's manual Jellyfin test matrix passes.
